# The genuine sheaf of closed native antiholomorphic one-forms

The closed-form equation is the actual symmetric antiholomorphic
coefficient-derivative equation in every original preferred chart.
Its locality, complex linearity, sheaf condition, inclusion into native
forms, and original scalar endomorphisms are proved.  No existence of
local primitives is assumed or included in the definition.
